From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Screensaver: a menu icon of its own and the game's sprites on
 the overlay

The main menu's Screensaver button shows a monitor with a park on it in place of
the play triangle (MenuIcon.h, generated by tools/mkmenuicon.py: runs of standard palette indices,
as the patched build replaces only the executables and cannot add to g2.dat). An overlay image's
src can be "sprite:<image index>": the sprite is drawn into a small render target and mapped
through the standard palette, so the mode can show the stock exit button whatever palette the
park sets; its own size is in game pixels.
---
